Falsifies `terminal_contract::verification::decode_answers_every_word_and_reads_it_back`.

The defect: the length is read as one less than the low word, which underflows on a request whose
length is zero. Every terminal server decodes through `decode`, so a zero-length write or a poll
would panic the terminal instead of being served.

Expected to fail: the subtraction's overflow check, on any word whose low 32 bits are zero.

diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
index a0b1ce1..1042e5e 100644
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -204,7 +204,7 @@ pub const fn operation(w0: u64) -> u64 {
 }
 /// The length/count of a request word.
 pub const fn len(w0: u64) -> usize {
-    (w0 & 0xffff_ffff) as usize
+    ((w0 & 0xffff_ffff) - 1) as usize
 }
 
 /// Bits 55:32 of a request's first word, which no operation gives a meaning.
